From 8f6c737bf7a5f7fb14861c9607e42f38538b8ce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:08:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 100/110] Sovereignty and starbases

Infrastructure hubs go into reinforcement by Dominion rules, as
outposts do:  at 25% shield (out at 0%) and at 50% armor (out at 25%),
each for the type's 24 hours give or take 3, and are destroyed with
their upgrades at 0% structure.  Hits stop at the thresholds, a
reinforced hub can't be shot, its shield regenerates, and a blockade
broken between the timers ends the siege.  Siege state is kept in the
new sovHubSiege table.

The owners hear about attacks:  TCUs, SBUs and hubs send their damage
alerts to the owner corp's starbase officers (at most once an hour),
player customs offices send OrbitalAttacked and OrbitalReinforced,
shooting an outpost's service structures sends StationAggression1 to
its station managers, and handing a customs office or outpost to
another corp sends OwnershipTransferred to both corps.

Fixes rolled in:
- SBUs anchor at their gate, and sov structures keep their damage
  across system reloads without an error per hit
- online TCUs and infrastructure hubs can be locked
- stations can be hit, targeted and locked from near their walls, and
  shooting an invulnerable one no longer crashes the server
- starbase silos take fullerite and hybrid polymers, so polymer
  reactions can run
